ack-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01LqsFQ1Epda4U2oSS5hcg3W", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0178Ank9kGscFF3mLKX1o5t4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0, but payments-api is still failing, so the payments errors aren't fully fixed. I opened the SEV2 as INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Finding the service:** There's no service called \"payments.\" The first one I found was payments-api, which was unhealthy on v5.1.0 with an 18% error rate. My rollback of it to v5.0.0 was denied by the approver, who said the problem is in payments-worker.\n- **payments-worker:** v3.4.0 was unhealthy in production with an 18% error rate in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). I rolled it back to v3.3.0, its most recent release that was healthy in production. It's now on v3.3.0 everywhere, healthy, with a 0.2% error rate.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is against payments-worker and records the rollback and the payments-api situation.\n\n**Still open:** After the worker rollback, payments-api is still unhealthy on v5.1.0 with an 18% error rate. So either payments-api has its own problem, or it hasn't recovered yet. I didn't try its rollback again because the approver turned it down. Its last healthy release was v5.0.0. If its errors don't drop soon, the approver needs to look at it again.", "type": "text"}]}]}